 page it's really  just where you go to download invoices  statements it used to be called the  invoices page it's been renamed and  cleaned up and again it's really just  about finding that data and downloading  it this is where you're gonna get the  hard copy for all those documents the  billing reports the actual chart that  you're seeing on the screen here this is  part of the billing reports page and  this is probably where you're gonna want  to spend most of your time right it  gives you a great way to visualize all  of the data that we were looking at  before the table is great because it  breaks down into great detail but it can  be a little hard to digest  right the visualization here is really  helpful and it shows you the  transactional costs on a per day basis  and you can actually break it between a  line chart and a bar chart but there's a  lot of options on this page and that's  where you'll be measuring a lot of your  costs so one of the new features here is  the cost forecast and this has been  added and changed a couple of times over  the past year and it includes long term  cost trends so now it includes up to 12  months and it factors in things like  sustained use discounts so sustained use  discounts will typically have a very  high it'll start off with a very low  discount and then as you go along this  is saying use discount kicks in and you  kind of get this down for its pattern  and then the next month starts and it  goes back up so the forecasting takes  all of that into effect and gives you a  great idea of where all that information  is and what you'll be spending over the  next 12 months in addition to that the  right side of the billing reports  there's all these filters on the right  side and you can drill down into any  specific components that you want when  you change these components it will  actually add it to the URL and then you  know if you make a custom report or  something you can just share that URL  with others so it's really easy to kind  of drill down into an area and then  share that with the rest of your team  there's also been a lot of new features  that have been added to the filters and  one of the cool ones is the invoice  centric view that you can click on so in  the default view you can kind of select  whatever range you want you know last 30  days 90 days or just custom ranges and  that's really helpful but the invoice  view just tailors it directly to your  invoice right so show me the invoice for  June show me the invoice for August or  Judaea August and again it breaks down  that chart so you can see the  information and the costs there but it  really just lets you say okay well  here's all the costs for that month and  how it compares to my invoice in  addition to that filter we've added a  couple other ones this one's really cool  it's location filter right so now you  can actually break down your cost by  where they came from what geography what  region or multi region area all of those  are available here just a really helpful  way to break down the costs in addition  to that we've got maples we talked about  project labels before and these are  resource labels where you're able to do  the same thing right let's let's take a  compute engine instance or multiple  instances and label them all with  production and  in the billing cost reports you can  actually say show me all those  production instances and the costs they  generated really really helpful to be  able to drill down into that level of  detail so I mentioned this before in the  in the health card but what you want to  do and here's a feature right you just  go to the billing reports page you  enable the export to bigquery and what  you want to do is turn that on if you  haven't done it so right now pause and  then go do it because it's really really  important it actually doesn't take data  from before you turn it on which is why  it's so important that you probably want  to go enable it now but this exports all  the billing data at a very granular  level some of the changes that have  happened recently is now that it's  hourly so it has a start hour in an end  hour and then it's all the costs that  have happened for all of the different  things associated with that billing  account it is the most granular data  you're gonna get and bigquery of course  is a great place to do giga analysis and  store data so it's really really helpful  to have that there but you can always  export it out of bigquery if you need to  hook it up to a third-party tool or bi  or whatever it's really helpful to have  and that's why it's so important to make  sure that you enable it because you're  gonna want to be able to see that level  of detail when you do any future cost  modeling or really just to get that  level of analysis on your costs so all  of that really focuses on the ways to  understand your costs I want to talk  about the biggest way to control your  costs right viewing them is great but  being able to control them is also very  important and we're going to talk about  budgets so budgets are probably the  number one tool to actually implement  cost controls and they're really  flexible they're actually very powerful  too so let's go ahead and break it down  starting with budgets the first thing  you can do is well you just kind of set  up a budget and when you set up a budget  say let's say a thousand dollar budget  when you hit that amount it's going to  send an email out to billing  administrators saying hey you hit this  budget but you can actually configure  multiple thresholds right because you  want to know maybe before you hit a  thousand dollars so when you set up a  budget you actually set a threshold and  you'll say fifty percent of a thousand  dollars and then 100 percent of a  thousand dollars but you can also set up  forecasted thresholds so forecasted  thresholds are about when Google Cloud  predicts that you're going to hit that  call  right and that can be really helpful to  stay on top of any surprises so if  you're three days into the month and you  get an email saying that hey Google  cloud thinks you're gonna spend 100% of  your thousand dollar budget that might  be a call to action to go do some of it  so as you set up a budget set up  multiple thresholds and you can set up  multiple budgets as well because you're  gonna want to be able to track different  things speaking of that you can actually  set up filters on the budget so the  budget by default is the entire billing  account but when you actually filter it  down you can choose specific projects  specific product or you can even choose  those resource labels that we talked  about earlier and say ok well show me  here's my production buddy here's my dev  budget here's the you know the budget  for all of my biz dev projects you have  that flexibility in that control to be  able to say well here we'll get  different alerts for different people  the other thing I want to talk about is  the budget API so this is currently in  beta but what it lets you do is automate  the creation and managing of those  budgets that's really important because  you know as you grow and your  organization gets more and more complex  you probably don't want to do all of  this by hand so being able to spend some  time learn the budget API it's really  really critical to being able to say ok  well I set up a new project we're gonna  go ahead and automate and add that to  budgets and creating your budgets and so  on so spending some time here can be  really valuable as you grow so we've  talked about budgets being able to send  out emails to billing administrators but  often times you want to send emails to  other people as well and that's where  this new feature comes in that can  actually let you add up to 5 emails per  budget through cloud monitoring and it's  actually pretty straightforward you just  go into the budget you click on the  little check box that says cloud  monitoring you're gonna set up a channel  and then you're just adding emails to  that an important note here is that you  know while you can just add five  individual emails you might want to  consider adding a group email instead  right so that way instead of sending it  to one person in accounting you're  sending it to a group in accounting or  to a biz dev team or whatever because  you want to be able to say here  send these budget alert emails to this  team but you don't want to have to  constantly add people to the team to the  budget right so it's much easier to  manage the team and something like gee  sweet and then just have that sent out  to that group and then you can kind of  leave the budgets alone so it's a great  way to add additional people to your  book  now that's the basics of budgets but the  real power of budgets come from what we  call programmatic budget notifications  and this is really cool because it  basically lets you hook up your budget  to pub/sub and pub/sub in in this case  is an event handler and it's gonna take  alerts from the budget and they'll send  them off to wherever you want to be and  we've got some sample code in the  documentation that actually looks at  sending it up to cloud functions but  when you when you create a budget you  just click that box very simple you  choose a pup subtopic or you make a new  one and then you can go off and make  your clock function and you know we've  got some sample code like I said a very  popular example of this is sending a  budget notification to slack right so  whenever you're an update when your  budget comes in go put it in a slack  Channel and have an update there simple  but it's just a notification so when you  have Google Cloud functions and other  systems in Google Cloud you can kind of  do whatever you could do with code and  that's really important because you can  actually do you know more advanced  things like let's say you hit a way  higher on your budget than you expected  you could actually shut down projects  you could shut down resources there's  some sample code for detaching a billing  account from a project that's a really  dangerous thing to do right because when  you remove the billing account for the  project any paid resources in that  project might get shut down in a very  unexpected way so be really careful  about that but it's a great starting  point to understand how do I really  control my resources and again it comes  down to your organization what's  important for your organization how do  those budgets come up for your  organization and then what kind of  responses can you have to really putting  controls in place so programmatic budget  notifications are really gonna be the  most powerful way to put cost controls  in your place so talked about  understanding talked about control let's  talk about optimizing cost right this is  the great one because basically you're  gonna end up saving money and hopefully  you're gonna do it without changing  anything and the first thing and  honestly the one of the more common  things I see is that people aren't  taking advantage of committed use  discounts and this is such a huge and  actually really easy thing to to set up  on your account all you have to do is  sign up for them and you'll start to pay  a lot less for some of the resources you  already use so commit use discounts or  sometimes we call them  HUD's are able to help you save on  really great static workloads so if  you've got you know V CPUs Ram SSDs GPUs  all of those at a static level you can  look at and say okay well I'm running a  good amount of that or I'd maybe I have  a baseline of it right you might have  spiky workloads but if you've got that  baseline you can take them out and  purchase a committed use discount for  that amount and then you're just gonna  be paying a lot less for the same thing  you're not changing those resources at  all you're just getting at this kind of  price because you're assigning up for a  one or three-year commitment based on  that so it's really helpful to have it's  really easy to set up and I've actually  just added in beta the committed use  discounts for cloud sequel right the  database is probably not something  you're spinning up and down a lot you  probably have a good baseline for that  so it's just another great way to save a  lot of money and we actually have the  committed use discount analysis report  now again available in the billing  section which lets you just visualize  your usage right so in this case you  have a very static usage it'll show you  what you're using on committed Hugh's  discounts what you could be using and  what's eligible for it and then you can  kind of say well look I've got this flat  workload that's gonna be running for a  year why don't I save money on very easy  way to save money and again no change is  really necessary to your actual  resources that are running so the other  thing that they changed in the last year  with committed use discounts is discount  sharing and this one is probably my  favorite because what it lets you do is  take committed use discounts and move  them to a billing and account level if  you've worked with them before they were  specific to a project right so you'd  have a committee just discount on this  project and one of this and this and  this and as you grow on projects that  can be pretty painful so it's really  great to be able to say all the billing  all the committee juice discounts are  now at the billing account level much  much easier and easier to say oh it's  just spread it across all of our  projects highly recommend you check that  out if you're using committed years  discounts because it's just an even  easier way to save money one of the  other features that's rolled out in  Allen is going to have a lot of changes  coming to it soon is the recommender hub  which is part of active assist it's  currently in beta and it surfaces a lot  of recommendations so you'll see some  security recommendations but you'll also  see some cost recommendations and two of  the great ones  a committed use discount recommendation  right so the analysis report lets you  see it but this one will just tell you  like hey look you're spending a lot here  you could be saving money there and then  another company recommendation is the  compute engine cross family  recommendations so when you're using  compute engine you've got a arrow eyes  which family are using in which sizes  you're using that can get pretty  complicated and this will basically  measure the the amount that you're using  those and say oh look this is a pretty  memory intensive application you're  running you might want to consider  switching to a memory optimized machine  and you'll end up saving a lot of money  there's a lot of great stuff coming to  the recommender hub so make sure to keep  your eye on that so with all of that  being said we talked about understanding  controlling and really optimizing your  cost there's two great sessions that are  also available this week CST 101 and CST  104 you can see a great customer story  of how they use these recommendations to  save money and a whole bunch of other  stuff definitely recommend you check  that out and if you're interested in  learning more you want to chat up to  this URL cloud.google.com slash cost  management because all of the resources  that we talked about and so much more  are there you've got resources guides  quick labs YouTube playlist a bunch of  stuff that really deep dives on these  individual topics so I know it was a lot  but thank you all so much for joining me  and don't forget to enable billing  export to bigquery thank you
 

